    "question": {
      "dom_id": "question-167221",
      "problem": "Find the minimum number of wooden tables the company needs to produce per week to make a weekly profit of $$4\\,800.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The company needs to produce$\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,$ wooden tables per week.",
      "worked_solution": "From part 5, the required number of wooden tables $x$ is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\n6\\cdot ({x}^{2}-60x+800)=0.\n$$\n\nDividing this equation by $6,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-60x+800=0.\n$$\n\nTo solve this equation, we want to find a factor pair of the constant term $(800)$ that also adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-60).$ The required factors are $(-20)$ and $(-40).$\n\nUsing this factor pair, we write the linear term as $-60x=-20x-40x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-60x+800 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-20x-40x+800 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-20x-40x+800 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-20x)+(-40x+800) & =0 \\\\ x(x-20)-40(x-20) & =0 \\\\ (x-20)(x-40)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the solutions are $x=20$ or $x=40.$ Since we require the minimum solution, we conclude that the company needs to produce $20$ wooden tables per week to make a profit of $$4\\,800.$",
      "problem_field_keys": [
        "field-1"
      ],
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
